    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0149" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg107"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 311.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 29, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Since the date of my despatch No. 301, I
                    have had some further correspondence with Lord Russell on the subject of the
                    steamer Georgiana Copies of the papers are herewith transmitted. It will be
                    perceived that the later materially contradicts the earlier testimony. In the
                    mean time the vessel departed. It is now boldly stated in the Liverpool
                    newspapers that she is to act as a tender to No. 290.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d66-a1.xml" xpointer="d66-a1"/>
            </div>
